//! The `wasm32` test registry for `temper-geometry`.
//!
//! Generated by `scripts/gen_wasm_test_registry.py`; run it after adding a
//! test to any listed module, and `--check` gates drift in CI.
//!
//! `cargo test`'s libtest harness cannot target `wasm32-unknown-unknown`,
//! so the Worker tier calls each test function individually instead of
//! running a test binary.  This module is the flat, indexable list of them.
//!
//! Only modules that survive `--no-default-features` appear here.  Tests
//! inside `#[cfg(feature = "python")]` modules are structurally absent
//! from a `wasm32` build and cannot be registered here at all.
//!
//! Two exclusion classes apply here, both structural:
//!
//! * `#[cfg(feature = "python")]` modules (`escape_via`, `zone_pour`,
//!   `geometry_kernels`, `congestion_tensor`, `fixed_copper`,
//!   `area_sufficiency`, `occupancy_raster`) do not exist in a
//!   `--no-default-features` build, so neither do their tests.
//! * `proptest` modules use a dev-dependency, which is not linked into
//!   the ordinary (non-test) build this registry compiles into.  The
//!   same exclusion `temper-drc-rs` makes for its own `proptests`
//!   modules.
//!
//! `scripts/gen_wasm_test_registry.py --crate temper-geometry --census`
//! prints the full module census with per-module counts.
//!
//! A `#[should_panic]` test panics by design, and on this target a panic
//! aborts into a trap -- indistinguishable over the C ABI from a genuine
//! failure.  Those tests stay registered and are listed in
//! `tools/wasm/wasm_expected_failures_geometry.json`, whose gate is
//! bidirectional: one that stops panicking is reported, not ignored.
//!
//! ## Families
//!
//! Each module entry in `ALL` is gated on a `wasm-registry-<family>`
//! feature, as in `temper-drc-rs`.  This crate is a flat set of
//! independent kernels with no rule-family taxonomy, so it declares a
//! single family (`geometry`) rather than inventing one; the mechanism
//! is in place if a size-driven split is ever wanted.

/// A single test: its fully qualified name and a nullary callable.
///
/// Failure is signalled by panicking, exactly as under libtest.  On
/// `wasm32-unknown-unknown` a panic aborts (the target has no unwinding on
/// stable), which surfaces to the host as a WebAssembly trap -- so the
/// runner catches the trap rather than a `Result`.
pub type WasmTest = (&'static str, fn());

